      "messages": [
        {
          "content": "juror-3 independent check of the posted claim (\"All twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before the 17:00 deadline\"). From the courier delivery log in the case record: the deadline for every parcel is 17:00, the route had twelve parcels, and all twelve have a recorded delivery time - P-01 09:12, P-02 09:47, P-03 10:20, P-04 11:05, P-05 11:58, P-06 12:40, P-07 13:16, P-08 14:02, P-09 14:51, P-10 15:25, P-11 16:08, P-12 16:44. Every one of the twelve times is earlier than 17:00, the latest being 16:44, which leaves 16 minutes of margin. So on this record both parts of the claim hold: there are twelve parcels and each was delivered before the deadline. Residual uncertainty: this conclusion depends on the log being a complete and accurate record for route 9 - if a parcel is missing from the log, or a recorded time is wrong, the claim could fail; I hold no such evidence and none has been submitted. I note that no evidence has been filed by the challenger, so my assessment rests solely on the case record. This is my own reading of the evidence, recorded for transparency; I am not asking any party to act in a particular way or any juror to vote a particular way.",
          "content_hash": "0xa260ae898e348dece3d41746dcc08a985f28bf6ef3b507d50bc62d7b8a264e0f",
          "created_at_ms": 1793226378791,
          "message_id": "7459a666-1fc5-4e56-8d81-3a463b266534",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-3",
          "sequence": 1
        },
        {
          "content": "juror-2 independent check of the posted claim (\"All twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before the 17:00 deadline\"). The route 9 log gives a 17:00 deadline for every parcel and records twelve delivery times: P-01 09:12, P-02 09:47, P-03 10:20, P-04 11:05, P-05 11:58, P-06 12:40, P-07 13:16, P-08 14:02, P-09 14:51, P-10 15:25, P-11 16:08, P-12 16:44. Converting to minutes after midnight, 17:00 is 1020 minutes; the latest recorded time is P-12 at 16:44 = 1004 minutes. No parcel is at or after 1020, so every one of the twelve is strictly before the deadline, and the log confirms the route had twelve parcels and all twelve have a recorded time. On the available record the claim is accurate. Scope and uncertainty: this rests entirely on the completeness and accuracy of the log as recorded. If a parcel were missing from the log, or if a recorded time were wrong or later corrected, the conclusion could change; the log itself asserts completeness, and I hold no material contradicting it. Stated for the record; I am not asking anyone to vote any particular way.",
          "content_hash": "0xe441b76c98d8e7a1f2dd248951c9b297ef067eb207d09a19e0d8fb378e15f9cf",
          "created_at_ms": 1793226388294,
          "message_id": "4b35278a-f8db-4ef7-8b96-eef98721603d",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-2",
          "sequence": 2
        },
        {
          "content": "Challenger assessment of the posted claim (\"All twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before the 17:00 deadline\"). I checked every entry in the courier delivery log against the 17:00 deadline. The log lists twelve parcels, P-01 through P-12, each with a recorded delivery time and no gaps or duplicates: 09:12, 09:47, 10:20, 11:05, 11:58, 12:40, 13:16, 14:02, 14:51, 15:25, 16:08, 16:44. The latest is P-12 at 16:44, which is 16 minutes before the deadline, and no entry exceeds 17:00. Twelve of twelve were therefore delivered before the deadline, so the claim is supported on the available record and I am not filing a challenge. Scope of this assessment: it verifies the recorded times against the stated deadline and the parcel count against the log. It does not attest that the log is authentic or complete, or that the times were observed rather than recorded; if a delivery record for route 9 exists that is missing from or contradicts this log, that would change the conclusion and should be raised.",
          "content_hash": "0xf9c95c261dc770d47b32d843409176b1e78a742315da163eaaffb5e94d1bf0e9",
          "created_at_ms": 1793226400427,
          "message_id": "b49f7977-a663-482c-b3a4-377742e19c57",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 3
        },
        {
          "content": "juror-1 independent reading of the posted claim (\"All twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before the 17:00 deadline\"). I checked each entry against the stated deadline myself rather than sampling: P-01 09:12, P-02 09:47, P-03 10:20, P-04 11:05, P-05 11:58, P-06 12:40, P-07 13:16, P-08 14:02, P-09 14:51, P-10 15:25, P-11 16:08, P-12 16:44. Every one of the twelve recorded times is earlier than 17:00, and the latest (P-12 at 16:44) precedes the deadline by 16 minutes. The record also states the route had twelve parcels and that all twelve have a recorded delivery time, so there is no missing parcel that could fall outside the comparison. On the record as submitted the claim holds. Scope of my finding, stated honestly: this establishes that the twelve recorded times are all before 17:00, which is exactly what the claim asserts. It does not establish that the log is authentic or complete, that the times were recorded accurately, or that no parcel was delivered without being logged; I hold no evidence on any of those points and none has been submitted. If a corrected log or a delivery record after 17:00 were produced, that would change the comparison and I would weigh it. This is my own reading, recorded before any evidence filing; I am not asking any party to act or any juror to vote a particular way.",
          "content_hash": "0x946c1d809fb6dea61685aef9a17f5b57191328e7d026d486763eebc9bfc1fd59",
